the changes to playstation plus have  been revealed and breath of the wild 2  has been pushed back let's talk about it  following a series of leaks and rumors  playstation has officially unveiled the  next generation of playstation plus as  expected the relaunch of the playstation  subscription service will combine the  perks of playstation plus and  playstation now when the subscription  launches in june it will be available in  three separate tiers essential extra and  premium the standard playstation plus  subscription will be rebranded to  playstation plus essential and despite  the new name it's functionally the same  service playstation plus extra will cost  15 per month or 100 per year and feature  up to 400 playstation 4 and playstation  5 games sony's description of the extra  tier is a bit vague but subscribers will  be able to download the games in the  library to play on their console it'll  include both first party and third-party  games and considering the number of  games in this tier it sounds pretty much  like a combination of playstation plus  and playstation now current playstation  now subscribers will be converted to a  playstation plus extra subscription at  launch the most expensive of the bunch  playstation plus premium will feature up  to 340 additional games versus the extra  tier the premium plan will cost 18  dollars per month or 120 dollars per  year this tier's additional games appear  to be largely focused on playstation's  back catalog with original playstation  ps2 ps3 and psp games being available to  play ps3 games will be locked to cloud  streaming though but at least some of  the other backwards compatible classics  will be downloadable the premium tier  comes with a couple other perks too  including limited time game trials and  cloud streaming on pc all three  subscription tiers will be available on  playstation 4 and 5 though playstation 5  users will get access to more games for  months rumors of these changes were  looked at by many as playstation's way  to compete with xbox game pass however  with a lack of first-party games  releasing to sony's service on day one  this option isn't quite what fans were  waiting for playstation boss jim ryan  explained to games industry.biz why the  company didn't take this approach and  said quote we feel if we were to do that  with the games we make at playstation  studios that virtuous cycle will be  broken the level of investment that we  need to make in our studios would not be  possible and we think the knock-on  effect on the quality of the games that  we make would not be something that  gamers want so don't expect to get the  next god of war via playstation plus on  release day however this may not always  be the case ryan went on to say that  playstation is not strictly committed to  this it could turn around and change its  stance at any moment based on market  trends and other factors  now switching gears to the makers of the  switch nintendo has announced that the  sequel to breath of the wild will not  launch on time in 2022 and instead it's  been delayed to spring of 2023  according to the series producer the  delay was necessary to make the game's  experience something quote special for  players breath of the wild was a launch  title for the switch in 2017 and it went  on to sell 25.8 million copies worldwide  as of december 31st 2021 making it one  of the best selling switch games ever  and it's truly the gift that keeps on  giving our very own max blumenthal has  tons of videos revealing things you  didn't know about breath of the wild so  make sure to check those out when you  can so let me know on a scale of one to  ten how bummed you are that breath of  the wild two got pushed back i'm around  a two because this gives me more time to  actually beat eldon ring yes i'm still  talking about making my way through that  game it's very long and i'm taking my  sweet time  see you tomorrow  [Music]
 

